@startuml seq_boot_interrupted
title SC-BOOT-05 - Programming interrupted, then recovered

participant "UDS tester" as Tester
participant "Plant model" as Plant
box "TCU"
participant "Application" as App
participant "PBL" as PBL
participant "SBL" as SBL
end box

note over Tester, SBL
Covers: SYS-BOOT-007, SYS-BOOT-001, SYS-BOOT-002, SYS-BOOT-008, SYS-BOOT-009, SYS-BOOT-013, SYS-BOOT-015, SYS-DIA-005,
SIM-TST-002, SIM-PLT-004, SG-06
UDS requests on DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, responses on DIAG_Resp 0x7E9 (can_matrix section 5).
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

note over Tester, SBL
Programming as in SC-BOOT-01 is running in the PBL or SBL programming session (steps 5 .. 19).
Steps 1 .. 4 run in the application: a stopped tester only ends the session (SYS-DIA-003, SC-DIA-01).
end note

alt reset or power loss
  note over PBL, SBL: the MCU resets during the sequence
else tester stops
  ... no request for S3 = 5000 ms in the programming session ...
  PBL -> PBL : the bootloader resets the MCU (SYS-BOOT-009)
end
note over PBL, SBL: reset: the SBL in RAM and the unlocked security state are discarded (SYS-BOOT-009)

alt interrupted in steps 5 .. 12 (before eraseMemory): application area unchanged
  PBL -> PBL : application check valid (SYS-BOOT-001), 50 ms boot window
  PBL -> App : start the previous application (SC-STA-01)
  note right of App: the unchanged previous application starts (SYS-BOOT-007)
  Tester -> App : 22 F1 81
  App --> Tester : 62 F1 81 <sw_version>
  Tester -> App : new sequence from step 1 (SC-BOOT-01)
else interrupted in step 19 (after 71 01 FF 01 00, before 51 01)
  PBL -> PBL : application check valid: header sector programmed after 0202 / FF01\npassed (SYS-BOOT-015, SYS-BOOT-001), 50 ms boot window
  PBL -> App : start the new, accepted application (SYS-BOOT-007)
else interrupted in steps 13 .. 18 (erase, download, checks before the positive response to 31 01 FF 01)
  note over PBL: the application header sector stays erased until 0202 and FF01\nof the application have passed (SYS-BOOT-015, reprogramming section 11)
  PBL -> PBL : application header sector erased, rest of the area erased or partially written:\nthe check completes without a processor fault (SYS-BOOT-013) -> invalid
  PBL -> PBL : stay in the bootloader, default session, no time limit (SYS-BOOT-002)
  note over PBL: no TCU_Actuators / TCU_Status (SYS-BOOT-008)
  Plant -> Plant : hydraulic default (SIM-PLT-004)
  note over Tester, SBL: Safe state of SG-06: bootloader, plant in the hydraulic default.

  == recovery: entry with an invalid application (reprogramming section 2) ==
  Tester -> PBL : 22 F1 81
  PBL --> Tester : 62 F1 81 FF FF FF FF
  note right of PBL: application invalid (SYS-DIA-005)
  Tester -> PBL : 10 02 (sent once)
  PBL --> Tester : 50 02 00 32 01 F4
  note right of PBL: PBL default -> programming session,\nno reset (reprogramming section 3)
  Tester -> PBL : steps 6 .. 11: 27 11 / 27 12, 34, 36 ..., 37, 31 01 02 02, 31 01 03 01
  SBL --> Tester : 71 01 03 01 00
  Tester -> SBL : steps 12 .. 18: 2E F1 5A, 31 01 FF 00, 34, 36 ..., 37, 31 01 02 02, 31 01 FF 01
  SBL --> Tester : 71 01 FF 01 00
  Tester -> SBL : step 19: 11 01
  SBL --> Tester : 51 01
  PBL -> PBL : application check valid (SYS-BOOT-001), 50 ms boot window
  PBL -> App : start the new application
  note right of App: a full new programming sequence succeeds (SYS-BOOT-007)
end

note over Tester, SBL: A power loss while the SBL writes boot info keeps the previous record (two slots A / B, reprogramming section 7).
@enduml
